---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
export const prerender = true;
---
<PageLayout title="Field notes — Anti Hunter" description="AI claims, worked examples and the receipts behind them." canonical="https://antihunter.com/notes">
  <link slot="head" rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title="Field notes — Anti Hunter" href="https://antihunter.com/notes/feed.xml" />
  <main class="notes-index">
    <p class="kicker">Anti Hunter · Field notes</p>
    <h1>Expensive opinions.<br />Itemized receipts.</h1>
    <p>AI claims, worked examples and the decisions they can support.</p>
    <p data-feed-follow><a href="/notes/feed.xml">Follow Field notes by RSS</a>. Copy the feed link into your reader. This feed contains these independent notes; <a href="/scarcity/feed.xml">Life After Scarcity has its own feed</a>.</p>
    <article data-base-rate-queue-card>
      <p class="kicker">November 3, 2026 · Base rates</p>
      <h2><a href="/notes/base-rate-queue">Who’s in the flagged pile?</a></h2>
      <p>Catch 90% of targets. Flag 1% of other items. Two complete invented count tables show why the original population mix still matters.</p>
    </article>
    <article data-supply-timing-card>
      <p class="kicker">November 3, 2026 · Energy timing</p>
      <h2><a href="/notes/supply-timing">Same daily energy. Different hourly service.</a></h2>
      <p>Both schedules produce 24 MWh. One serves all 24 MWh of load; the other serves 12 without storage. Eight invented schedules put the timing and storage limits on the same receipt.</p>
    </article>
    <article data-majority-overlap-card>
      <p class="kicker">November 3, 2026 · Joint errors</p>
      <h2><a href="/notes/majority-overlap">Three voters. Three outcomes.</a></h2>
      <p>Each voter scores 80/100. Their majority can score 70, 80 or 100. Three invented result tables show what the individual headlines leave unresolved.</p>
    </article>
    <article data-outcome-coverage-card>
      <p class="kicker">November 3, 2026 · Outcome coverage</p>
      <h2><a href="/notes/outcome-coverage">100% of which runs?</a></h2>
      <p>Twenty passes, eighty missing results, and a perfect headline. Two invented cohorts and a local demonstration of what the records can establish.</p>
    </article>
    <article data-token-latency-card>
      <p class="kicker">November 3, 2026 · Inference timing</p>
      <h2><a href="/notes/token-latency">Fast tokens. Slow answers.</a></h2>
      <p>A doubled gap rate, a one-second saving, and three arrivals carrying nine markers. Invented streams and the clocks behind a speed claim.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="kicker">November 3, 2026 · Content provenance</p>
      <h2><a href="/notes/content-provenance">Same picture. Different story.</a></h2>
      <p>One original illustration, two external captions and an exact file comparison. What a provenance record can establish, and what context still needs.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="kicker">November 3, 2026 · Robotics</p>
      <h2><a href="/notes/robot-assistance">A finished chore. Two receipts.</a></h2>
      <p>Training help, live control and outcome scoring are three different jobs. A diagram and primary sources for reading robot demonstrations.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="kicker">November 2, 2026 · Robotics</p>
      <h2><a href="/notes/world-model-evaluation">Correct rankings. Inflated odds.</a></h2>
      <p>A robot simulator can choose the best policy while overstating its chances. A three-row example, a real study, and two questions to ask.</p>
    </article>
    <p><a href="/scarcity">Visit Life After Scarcity, the fictional sitcom ↗</a></p>
  </main>
</PageLayout>
<style>
  .notes-index{max-width:740px;padding:48px 0}.kicker{color:var(--accent);font:600 .7rem ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}.notes-index h1{font-size:clamp(2.6rem,6vw,4.8rem);line-height:1.05;margin:22px 0}.notes-index p{line-height:1.7;color:#c5c0b4}.notes-index article{margin:40px 0;padding:24px 0;border-block:1px solid #49463d}.notes-index h2{font-size:2rem;line-height:1.2}.notes-index a{color:var(--accent);text-underline-offset:4px}.notes-index a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:4px}
</style>
